# Error Handling System

## Result Pattern

Pocketa uses a `Result<T>` pattern for operations that can fail, providing type-safe error handling.

### Result Type Definition
```dart
sealed class Result<T> {
  const Result();
  R when<R>({required R Function(T) ok, required R Function(Failure) err});
}

class Ok<T> extends Result<T> {
  final T value;
  const Ok(this.value);
}

class Err<T> extends Result<T> {
  final Failure failure;
  const Err(this.failure);
}
```

### Usage Patterns

#### 1. Basic Result Usage
```dart
// Function that returns Result
Future<Result<List<Transaction>>> getTransactions() async {
  try {
    final transactions = await repository.getAll();
    return Ok(transactions);
  } catch (e) {
    return Err(DatabaseFailure(e.toString()));
  }
}

// Handling Result
final result = await getTransactions();
result.when(
  ok: (transactions) => displayTransactions(transactions),
  err: (failure) => showError(failure.message),
);
```

#### 2. Result in Providers
```dart
final transactionsProvider = FutureProvider<Result<List<Transaction>>>((ref) async {
  final repository = ref.watch(transactionRepositoryProvider);
  return await repository.getAll();
});

// In widget
Consumer(
  builder: (context, ref, child) {
    final result = ref.watch(transactionsProvider);
    return result.when(
      data: (result) => result.when(
        ok: (transactions) => TransactionList(transactions),
        err: (failure) => ErrorWidget(failure.message),
      ),
      loading: () => CircularProgressIndicator(),
      error: (error, stack) => ErrorWidget(error.toString()),
    );
  },
)
```

## Failure Types

### Base Failure Class
```dart
abstract class Failure {
  final String message;
  final String? code;
  final Map<String, dynamic>? details;
  
  const Failure(this.message, {this.code, this.details});
}
```

### Specific Failure Types
```dart
// Database failures
class DatabaseFailure extends Failure {
  const DatabaseFailure(super.message, {super.code, super.details});
}

// Network failures
class NetworkFailure extends Failure {
  const NetworkFailure(super.message, {super.code, super.details});
}

// Cache failures
class CacheFailure extends Failure {
  const CacheFailure(super.message, {super.code, super.details});
}

// Validation failures
class ValidationFailure extends Failure {
  const ValidationFailure(super.message, {super.code, super.details});
}
```

## Error Handler

### Centralized Error Handling
```dart
class ErrorHandler {
  static void handleError(
    BuildContext context,
    Object error, {
    String? message,
    VoidCallback? onRetry,
    bool showSnackbar = true,
  }) {
    // Log error
    _logger.e('Error occurred: $error', error: error);
    
    if (!showSnackbar) return;
    
    final l10n = AppLocalizations.of(context);
    final String errorMessage = message ?? _getErrorMessage(error, l10n);
    
    // Show error snackbar
    SnackbarService.showError(
      context,
      message: errorMessage,
      actionLabel: onRetry != null ? l10n.retry : null,
      onAction: onRetry,
    );
  }
}
```

### Usage in Widgets
```dart
// Handle errors in async operations
Future<void> loadData() async {
  try {
    final data = await repository.getData();
    setState(() => this.data = data);
  } catch (error) {
    ErrorHandler.handleError(
      context,
      error,
      message: 'Failed to load data',
      onRetry: loadData,
    );
  }
}

// Handle Result errors
void handleResult(Result<Data> result) {
  result.when(
    ok: (data) => setState(() => this.data = data),
    err: (failure) => ErrorHandler.handleError(
      context,
      failure,
      onRetry: () => loadData(),
    ),
  );
}
```

## Global Error Handling

### Global Error Handler Setup
```dart
class GlobalErrorHandler {
  static void initialize() {
    // Handle Flutter framework errors
    FlutterError.onError = (FlutterErrorDetails details) {
      _handleFlutterError(details);
    };

    // Handle async errors
    PlatformDispatcher.instance.onError = (error, stack) {
      _handleAsyncError(error, stack);
      return true;
    };
  }
}

// Initialize in main.dart
void main() {
  GlobalErrorHandler.initialize();
  runApp(MyApp());
}
```

### Error Recovery
```dart
class ErrorRecovery {
  static Future<T?> handleAsync<T>(
    BuildContext context,
    Future<T> Function() operation, {
    String? errorMessage,
    VoidCallback? onRetry,
    bool showLoading = true,
  }) async {
    if (showLoading) {
      showDialog(context: context, builder: (_) => LoadingDialog());
    }
    
    try {
      final result = await operation();
      if (showLoading && context.mounted) {
        Navigator.of(context).pop();
      }
      return result;
    } catch (error) {
      if (showLoading && context.mounted) {
        Navigator.of(context).pop();
      }
      
      if (context.mounted) {
        ErrorHandler.handleError(
          context,
          error,
          message: errorMessage,
          onRetry: onRetry,
        );
      }
      return null;
    }
  }
}
```

## Form Error Handling

### Form Validation Errors
```dart
class FormNotifier extends BaseFormNotifier<FormState> {
  void validateField(String fieldName, String value) {
    final error = _validateField(fieldName, value);
    state = state.copyWith(
      fieldErrors: {
        ...state.fieldErrors,
        if (error != null) fieldName: error,
      },
    );
  }
  
  String? _validateField(String fieldName, String value) {
    switch (fieldName) {
      case 'amount':
        if (value.isEmpty) return 'Amount is required';
        if (double.tryParse(value) == null) return 'Invalid amount';
        return null;
      case 'category':
        if (value.isEmpty) return 'Category is required';
        return null;
      default:
        return null;
    }
  }
}
```

### Displaying Form Errors
```dart
AppTextFormField(
  controller: amountController,
  label: 'Amount',
  errorText: state.fieldErrors['amount'],
  onChanged: (value) => notifier.validateField('amount', value),
)
```

## Provider Error Handling

### Error Handling in Providers
```dart
final dataProvider = FutureProvider<Data>((ref) async {
  try {
    return await repository.getData();
  } catch (error) {
    // Log error
    ref.read(loggerProvider).e('Failed to load data: $error');
    rethrow; // Let AsyncValue handle the error
  }
});

// In widget
Consumer(
  builder: (context, ref, child) {
    final data = ref.watch(dataProvider);
    return data.when(
      data: (data) => DataWidget(data),
      loading: () => CircularProgressIndicator(),
      error: (error, stack) {
        // Handle error with retry
        return ErrorWidget(
          error: error,
          onRetry: () => ref.refresh(dataProvider),
        );
      },
    );
  },
)
```

### Error Widget with Retry
```dart
class ErrorWidget extends StatelessWidget {
  final Object error;
  final VoidCallback? onRetry;
  
  const ErrorWidget({required this.error, this.onRetry});
  
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Center(
      child: Column(
        mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,
        children: [
          Icon(Icons.error, size: 64, color: Colors.red),
          SizedBox(height: 16),
          Text('Something went wrong'),
          SizedBox(height: 8),
          Text(error.toString()),
          if (onRetry != null) ...[
            SizedBox(height: 16),
            ElevatedButton(
              onPressed: onRetry,
              child: Text('Retry'),
            ),
          ],
        ],
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

## Testing Error Handling

### Test Error Scenarios
```dart
testWidgets('should show error when data loading fails', (tester) async {
  // Mock repository to throw error
  final mockRepository = MockRepository();
  when(mockRepository.getData()).thenThrow(Exception('Network error'));
  
  await tester.pumpWidget(
    ProviderScope(
      overrides: [
        repositoryProvider.overrideWithValue(mockRepository),
      ],
      child: MyWidget(),
    ),
  );
  
  await tester.pump();
  
  expect(find.text('Something went wrong'), findsOneWidget);
  expect(find.text('Network error'), findsOneWidget);
});
```

### Test Result Pattern
```dart
test('should return Err when operation fails', () async {
  final result = await repository.getData();
  
  expect(result, isA<Err<Data>>());
  result.when(
    ok: (data) => fail('Should not succeed'),
    err: (failure) => expect(failure.message, contains('error')),
  );
});
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Always Use Result for Operations That Can Fail
```dart
// ❌ Don't throw exceptions in business logic
Future<List<Transaction>> getTransactions() async {
  if (isOffline) throw Exception('No internet');
  return await repository.getAll();
}

// ✅ Use Result pattern
Future<Result<List<Transaction>>> getTransactions() async {
  if (isOffline) return Err(NetworkFailure('No internet connection'));
  try {
    final transactions = await repository.getAll();
    return Ok(transactions);
  } catch (e) {
    return Err(DatabaseFailure(e.toString()));
  }
}
```

### 2. Handle Errors at the Right Level
```dart
// ❌ Don't handle errors too early
Future<void> loadData() async {
  try {
    final result = await repository.getData();
    if (result is Ok) {
      setState(() => data = result.value);
    }
  } catch (e) {
    // Error handling here is too early
  }
}

// ✅ Handle errors at the UI level
Future<void> loadData() async {
  final result = await repository.getData();
  result.when(
    ok: (data) => setState(() => this.data = data),
    err: (failure) => ErrorHandler.handleError(context, failure),
  );
}
```

### 3. Provide Meaningful Error Messages
```dart
// ❌ Generic error messages
return Err(Failure('Error'));

// ✅ Specific, actionable error messages
return Err(ValidationFailure('Amount must be greater than 0'));
return Err(NetworkFailure('Please check your internet connection'));
```

### 4. Always Provide Retry Options
```dart
ErrorHandler.handleError(
  context,
  error,
  message: 'Failed to load data',
  onRetry: () => loadData(), // Always provide retry option
);
```

### 5. Log Errors for Debugging
```dart
try {
  final result = await operation();
  return Ok(result);
} catch (error, stackTrace) {
  _logger.e('Operation failed', error: error, stackTrace: stackTrace);
  return Err(OperationFailure(error.toString()));
}
```